      "rationale": "The CHANGELOG shows several deliberate recent changes but none documents touching `TokenList._token_matching`'s reverse-search index math, which uses `range(start - 2, -2, -1)`. Since the stop bound `-2` is exclusive, the range includes `-1`, and Python resolves `tokens[-1]` to the *last* element instead of signalling \"out of range\", so `token_prev` called at index 0 wrongly returns the statement's last token instead of `(None, None)` as its own docstring promises. This single bug cascades into `StripCommentsFilter` (which checks `prev_ is None` to decide whether a leading comment can be deleted cleanly) and into `ReindentFilter._split_statements` (whose own comment says \"only break if it's not the first token\"), producing a stray leading blank line in both `strip_comments` and `reindent` output \u2014 matching the reported failing checks (\"strip comments single/multi\", \"reindent: stmts\"). The expected values come straight from `TokenList.token_prev`'s docstring, from the self-evident intent of the `prev_ is None` branches in the source, and from the long-standing worked example in `docs/source/intro.rst`, so they reflect intended behavior rather than whatever the buggy code currently emits.",
